# Who must review what.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: a review gate is the only control that matches the actual risk here. Cluster
# configs are not just "a config" — `charts/cluster-base` renders ClusterSecretStores that read the
# vault, Karpenter node classes that create VMs, and workloads that run with the cluster's credentials.
# A manual approval button would only gate WHEN such code runs; this gates WHAT it can be.
#
# Owner: the repository owner, so nothing in these trees merges without them.

# The cluster factory: the module every cluster root calls, and the charts each cluster applies.
/terraform/            @Hnatekmar
/charts/               @Hnatekmar
/bootstrap/            @Hnatekmar

# The lifecycle scripts — apply, bootstrap, wire-vault, teardown. Teardown destroys infrastructure, so
# it is in the same class as the code that creates it.
/scripts/tofu-ci.sh            @Hnatekmar
/scripts/bootstrap-cluster.sh  @Hnatekmar
/scripts/teardown-cluster.sh   @Hnatekmar
/scripts/wire-vault.sh         @Hnatekmar
/scripts/kubeconfig.sh         @Hnatekmar

# The workflows themselves: editing one can change what may be applied where.
/.github/workflows/    @Hnatekmar
/.github/actions/      @Hnatekmar
